zink/st: Metal objects through GL interop, callback after a flush

1. zink enables VK_EXT_metal_objects when available and implements the
   GL interop hook interop_export_object: MesaGLInteropEGLExportObject
   on a texture returns the MTLDevice, MoltenVK's MTLCommandQueue (the
   one zink submits to) and the texture's MTLTexture (new struct
   mesa_glinterop_metal_objects in mesa_glinterop.h), no dmabuf.
2. MesaGLInteropRunAfterFlush(fn, data) flushes the current context
   asynchronously and runs fn on the threaded context's driver thread
   after that flush. zink's flush returns only after vkQueueSubmit,
   which MoltenVK commits synchronously, so Metal work committed in fn
   runs after the GL commands issued so far and before later ones,
   without a CPU wait for the GPU.

OpenMW's MetalFX upscaling needs the Metal textures behind GL textures
and Metal work in GL command order on the same queue; zink had no
interop hook on Apple platforms. Limits: the exported objects are not
retained (valid while the GL texture keeps its storage), and ordering
relies on MoltenVK's default synchronous queue submits. Non-Metal
builds are unchanged.

Upstream: not submitted.

--- a/include/GL/mesa_glinterop.h
+++ b/include/GL/mesa_glinterop.h
@@ -443,6 +443,26 @@
                                                    unsigned count, struct mesa_glinterop_export_in *resources,
                                                    struct mesa_glinterop_flush_out *out);
 
+/**
+ * Driver data of the export functions (out_driver_data) for zink on Metal (MoltenVK): the Metal objects behind
+ * the exported texture. Not retained: valid while the GL object exists and keeps its storage.
+ */
+struct mesa_glinterop_metal_objects {
+   uint32_t version;        /* 1 */
+   void *mtl_device;        /* id<MTLDevice> */
+   void *mtl_command_queue; /* id<MTLCommandQueue> the driver submits to */
+   void *mtl_texture;       /* id<MTLTexture> */
+};
+
+/**
+ * Calls fn(data) once the GL commands issued so far in the current context are submitted to the driver's queue
+ * (MoltenVK: committed to its MTLCommandQueue), before any later GL command is. Work committed to that queue in
+ * fn therefore executes in GL command order. Flushes asynchronously, does not wait for the GPU; fn may run on
+ * another thread.
+ */
+void
+MesaGLInteropRunAfterFlush(void (*fn)(void *data), void *data);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
